s a scholar after after that  you know i won't even say what i think  it is  so euro rumor has a question for me  about raising my kids  and and faith he says uh did you raise  them or are you currently raising them  as christians if so how did you  or or do you keep them open and free  thinkers  so it's interesting that you know the  the  background assumption should be that if  you're actually doing some sort of  religious education  or talking in any meaningful way about  faith and not just doing so in the kind  of religious studies well here's what  these people think here's what these  people think  that you're sort of indoctrinating them  or  or keeping them from being able to  develop openness  so first off whether even if we take the  religion off the table  if you don't teach something substantive  you actually preclude the possibility of  open-mindedness  because you need this is the way  people's minds develop you need to  actually grapple with things  and to be able to take a critical  position on them if all you have is some  vague  you know notions about it you can't even  really take a critical position on it  another way of putting this is in very  practical terms is  it's good to teach you know something so  that kids actually have something to  react and rebel against  now it is possible to teach in kind of a  brainwashing fashion and i've seen  people do that  and i've seen them do that in all sorts  of denominations and i've seen people do  that who are atheists as well  i personally think and this is part of  why i belong to the christian  intellectual tradition that  if you're actually using your mind the  way that god wants you to be using your  mind  you're not going to be brainwashed  yourself and you're not going to be  brainwashing anybody else you are in  fact going to be  inculcating in them a real love for the  truth that will lead them  to to you know try to figure out what  what's what  and um yeah that's probably enough about  that  